#edb/ref 17592186094773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186094774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186094775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186094776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094771 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094771 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094771 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eeb17fdb-d008-5d2a-befe-3afdce935947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094772 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}(t^{3} - 1)(t^{2} - t)dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094772 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094772 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eada6d87-e15d-59b5-9b10-60f77bcee43f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094773 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}(t^{3} - t)(t^{2} - t)dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094773 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094773 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fc88212e-1ae9-522e-8d83-f5da9c66fb29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094774 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}t(t^{3} - t^{2})(t^{2} - 1)dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094774 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094774 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3bc5dc3a-89b2-5658-8363-a30bfa05702d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094775 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}t(t^{3} - 1)(t^{2} - 1)dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094775 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094775 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "46abf8b7-761a-5309-87bb-491ad91f0611" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094776 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}(t^{3} - t)(t^{2} - 1)dt" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094776 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186094776 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b055023-d423-55ec-8127-24ff67ebbfa6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096538 #edb/ref 1069 "e-604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096538 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e9/e933e484b931ee54b345a8e7af3b0e44f80a8b019e3e401007ad4987192e33be.png)\n\nFind the area bounded between the curve defined parametrically as\n$x = t^2 - 1, \\qquad y = t^3 - 4t$\nand the $x$-axis for $t \\in [-2,0]$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "85879186-0866-5159-905b-65d043681231" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096538 #edb/ref 1074 "The unsigned area bounded by the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx = x(t), \\qquad y = y(t), \\qquad t_1 \\leq t \\leq t_2\n$$\n\nand the $x$-axis is given by the absolute value of the integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{t_1}^{t_2} y \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t} \\:\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dt} &= \\frac{d}{dt}(t^{2} - 1) \\\\\n&= 2t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the integral expression\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}y\\frac{dx}{dt}dt &= \\int_{-2}^{0}(t^{3} - 4t)(2t)dt \\\\\n&= 2\\int_{-2}^{0}t^{2}(t^{2} - 4)dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that this integral will give us a negative number since\n\n$$\ny\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t} \\leq 0\n$$\n\nfor all $t \\in [-2,0]$.\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= -2\\int_{-2}^{0}t^{2}(t^{2} - 4)dt \\\\\n&= 2\\int_{-2}^{0}t^{2}(4 - t^{2})dt \\\\\n&= 2\\int_{-2}^{0}(4t^{2} - t^{4})dt \\\\\n&= 8\\int_{-2}^{0}t^{2}dt - 2\\int_{-2}^{0}t^{4}dt \\\\\n&= 8 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{t^{3}}{3}\\right|_{-2}^{0} - 2 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{t^{5}}{5}\\right|_{-2}^{0} \\\\\n&= 8(\\frac{0^{3}}{3} - ((-2)^{3})/(3)) - 2(\\frac{0^{5}}{5} - ((-2)^{5})/(5)) \\\\\n&= 8(\\frac{8}{3}) - 2(\\frac{32}{5}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{64}{3} - \\frac{64}{5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{128}{15}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096561 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7412" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096561 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/3d/3dd84b2e84056a4e6c71f7b76534f5a6f1a46132ea5da5ed8edb2a514b9ea6b4.png)\n\nFind an integral expression for the area bounded between the curve defined parametrically as\n$x = e^{-t^2}, \\qquad y = t^3$,\nand the $x$-axis for $0 \\leq t \\leq \\sqrt{2} \\,$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "95cdc31d-c3f2-50b6-9447-b7317af775f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096561 #edb/ref 1074 "The unsigned area bounded by the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx = x(t), \\qquad y = y(t), \\qquad t_1 \\leq t \\leq t_2\n$$\n\nand the $x$-axis is given by the absolute value of the integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{t_1}^{t_2} y \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t} \\:\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dx}{dt} &= \\frac{d}{dt}(e^{-t^{2}}) \\\\\n&=-2te^{-t^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the integral expression\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}y\\frac{dx}{dt}dt &= \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t^{3}(-2te^{-t^{2}})dt \\\\\n&=-2\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t^{4}e^{-t^{2}}dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that this integral will give us a negative number since\n\n$$\ny\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t} \\leq 0\n$$\n\nfor all $t \\in [0, \\sqrt{2}]$.\n\nTherefore, the area is given by\n\n$$\nA = -\\left(-2 \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}} t^4 e^{-t^2} \\, \\textrm{d}t \\right) = 2 \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}} t^4 e^{-t^2} \\, \\textrm{d}t\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096731 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186096926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096731 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186527964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096731 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Area Bounded by a Parametric Curve" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096731 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096731 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f354f758-3745-5cee-9a4b-a0878c2c8578" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096758 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096758 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096758 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding an Integral Expression for the Area Bounded by a Parametric Curve" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096758 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096758 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f20da72e-5a93-5a4e-be39-d412bd8fee86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating Areas Bounded by Parametric Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096851 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "71e9c379-9817-5da3-85f9-50847626fa5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097133 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186094771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097133 #edb/ref 1069 "q-15688" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097133 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/3b/3bde5b93aa28654977fdb55b0b2808fde2fb2f54ba33a6e9a2a4281b6966682f.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the area bounded between the curve defined parametrically as\n$x = t^{4} - 2t^{2}, y = t^{3} - 1$\nand the $x$-axis for $t ∈ [1, \\sqrt{2}]$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097133 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad65213f-7896-5eb3-8900-a92c0319ea40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097612 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097612 #edb/ref 1061 2136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097612 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "786032d8-d66a-579e-8336-348ca609cfb8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097612 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097613 #edb/ref 1061 2138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097613 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "296a64b2-a271-5186-bf37-e47d7b56624c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097613 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097653 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097653 #edb/ref 1061 27495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097653 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a032caf-6330-5e24-bafb-d45c348ad375" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097653 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097747 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097747 #edb/ref 1061 45599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097747 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "97757635-74ae-5269-ac75-2ea85021adb9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097747 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097798 #edb/ref 1064 "![](images/d8/d8f08b1cc474cfee367ccf52e2299deaeec146ef7a7a860f64a75f7f7f25cb0b.png)\n\nConsider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^3-1, \\qquad y=2t-t^3, \\qquad t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)\n$$\n\nThe shaded area shown in the diagram is the finite region bounded between the curve, the $x$-axis, and the vertical lines formed by $x$-axis and the points on the curve corresponding to $t_1=0$ to $t_2=1$, as shown.\n\nWe know that the area of the curve is given by\n\n$$\nA = \\int_{a}^{b} y \\:\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nSince our curve is defined parametrically, we need to change the variable of integration from $x$ to $t$ using the change of variables formula, given by\n\n$$\nA = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} y(t) \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm d t}\\:\\textrm d t\n$$\n\nNow, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(t^{3} - 1) = 3t^{2}\n$$\n\nApplying the change of variables formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}y(t)\\frac{dx}{dt}dt \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}(2t - t^{3}) \\cdot 3t^{2}dt \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}6t^{3} - 3t^{5}dt \\\\\n&= 6\\int_{0}^{1}t^{3}dt - 3\\int_{0}^{1}t^{5}dt \\\\\n&= 6 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{t^{4}}{4}\\right|_{0}^{1} - 3 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{t^{6}}{6}\\right|_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= 6(\\frac{1}{4} - 0) - 3(\\frac{1}{6} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shaded area shown in the picture has an area of $1$ square unit." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097798 #edb/ref 1065 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097798 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1d0c890f-fbe0-5ded-948b-b94d13caac3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097798 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097915 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, the area between the $x$-axis and the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx = x(t), \\qquad y = y(t), \\qquad t_1 \\leq t \\leq t_2\n$$\n\nis given by the absolute value of the integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{t_1}^{t_2} y \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t} \\:\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- When applying this formula, we assume that the chosen parametrization traverses the curve only once.\n- It's possible that this integral gives a negative value for the area even when the corresponding region lies entirely above the $x$-axis! To see why, note that if the curve lies above the $x$-axis, we must have $y(t) > 0$. However, if the curve is parameterized so that it is traversed from right to left, then $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t} < 0$, and we have\n$y\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t} < 0$\nand thus, our integral turns out to be negative.\n- To ensure that we get an unsigned area, we take the absolute value of the integral.\n- In general, care must be taken when asked to compute the area bounded by a parametric curve when $y\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t}$ changes sign over the domain of integration. However, we won't consider that scenario here.\n\nLet's see another example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097915 #edb/ref 1065 7915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097915 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "89e96b74-e406-52f5-b64e-46267df927e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097915 #edb/ref 1067 "A General Formula for the Area Bounded by a Parametric Curve" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
